WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.817
STEPHANIE WONG: This
week, we're talking

00:00:01.817 --> 00:00:04.980
about data storage, Anthos, and
eagerly anticipating next year.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:05.820
I'm Stephanie Wong.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.280
And welcome to the
last 2019 episode

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:11.340
of "This Week in Cloud," where
we serve you the lowest latency

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:12.270
news

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.040
There's a ton of data out
there, and the more you have,

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.740
the harder it can be to move.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.780
Google Cloud's Storage
Transfer Service

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.690
can help you move terabytes
of data from anywhere

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:22.780
to the Cloud.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:25.560
And now in beta, you can even
move your data from on-prem

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.770
with the same set of tools.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:29.520
Two of the biggest
announcements this year

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.350
were Anthos and Cloud Run.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:33.997
But these two work
even better together.

00:00:33.997 --> 00:00:35.580
There's a whole bunch
of new features,

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.230
like traffic
management and on-prem

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.120
support that come with Anthos.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.550
And you can even try it for
free until May next year.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.120
Cloud Run is the easiest
way to run containers.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.442
But what if your app
isn't containerized?

00:00:47.442 --> 00:00:48.900
It's time to
modernize with Migrate

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.910
for Anthos, which can
help you transform

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.920
your virtual machines
into containers,

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.480
no matter where they're hosted.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.400
Check out the guides, and
try these out for yourself.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.340
2019 has been a busy year.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.980
We've seen all kinds of
exciting announcements,

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:05.190
like the new features being
added to Kubernetes and Anthos

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.770
or around the exciting
AI and ML updates that

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.292
make it even easier for you
to create your own models.

00:01:10.292 --> 00:01:12.000
The busiest time this
year was all around

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.790
Google Cloud Next with
different talks, demos,

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.410
and lots of great showcases.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.990
And I'm sure next year,
it will be even busier.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:20.538
On behalf of the
team here, thank you

00:01:20.538 --> 00:01:22.080
for checking out
"This Week in Cloud"

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.850
to stay up to date
with the latest.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.627
2020 has so much more
to come, so stay tuned.

00:01:26.627 --> 00:01:28.710
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.930
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:33.580
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.890
We'll see you in
the Cloud next year.

